a21937d9-3017-4884-a30d-b4ee49dea8cf	7 DAYS TO GO ✨	7 DAYS TO GO ✨\n\nThe countdown to Central Mindanao University’s 115th Founding Anniversary and Alumni Homecoming begins! 💚💛\n\n7 DAYS TO GO ✨\n\nThe countdown to Central Mindanao University’s 115th Founding Anniversary and Alumni Homecoming begins! 💚💛\n\n📍 Today’s spotlight: \nMusuan Peak (Mt. Kalayo) 🌋\n\n𝗗𝗶𝗱 𝘆𝗼𝘂 𝗸𝗻𝗼𝘄? Musuan Peak is an active volcano that rises 646 meters high with a 3-kilometer base, home to 524 plant species. In 1976, PHIVOLCS recorded a strong seismic swarm here. But beyond its geology, what makes Musuan Peak truly fascinating are the stories behind its name and formation.\n\n🌿 From epic to myth:\nAccording to the epic Olaging, Musuan Peak was formed from the feces of Pugak, the nephew of Agyu. As the family of Agyu journeyed through the mountains, they stopped to rest and eat. Pugak, being greedy, ate more food than the others. Soon after, his stomach began to ache badly. Unable to hold it in, he defecated right while in heaven, and his feces became a mountain, now known as Musuan Peak.\n\n⛰️\nThe name "Musuan" is believed to have originated from a foreigner who visited the place and was accompanied by the natives. When the foreigner arrived at the top of the peak, in utter amazement at the view, he exclaimed, “The most one.” He found everything very beautiful from the top. The natives kept repeating what he said, but because they couldn’t speak it the way that he did, they pronounced it instead as “mus-wan.” Later on, this became the name of the peak, thus Musuan Peak. \n\n⛰️\nFor students of Central Mindanao University (CMU), Musuan Peak holds a special significance. A long-standing campus myth claims that students must climb the mountain to graduate, making it a symbolic rite of passage for CMUans. While the myth may not be true, it has become part of the university's culture.\n\n🌄\nToday, Musuan Peak is a popular destination for students, teachers, and tourists. The peak offers stunning views, and its slopes are home to a variety of flora and fauna. Visitors can explore the Mount Musuan Zoological and Botanical Garden, which features a butterfly greenhouse and a reforestation nursery.\n\n💭 Do you know other stories about Musuan Peak? Share them with us in the comments!\n\n📅 Full Schedule of Activities for CMU at 115 will be posted  soon.\n\n👉 Register now https://tinyurl.com/cmu115reg\n\n#CMUat115 #CMUFoundingAnniversary #MusuanPeak #MtKalayo #CMUans	Update	Medium	All	https://scontent.fcgy3-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/545570364_1208120451360280_3124857218412535803_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_p720x720_tt6&_nc_cat=111&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=7b2446&_nc_ohc=ClgEQDH7Z-gQ7kNvwFkjwPG&_nc_oc=Ado0EP2B_2bW3D663ABZvEVh5HAkVFyeq9Znc1nHqUqROa84ERrLmk3JG8tpE7ssp6U&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy3-1.fna&edm=AKIiGfEEAAAA&_nc_gid=vkb6lpMGbFtyr5HUL1YbKg&_nc_tpa=Q5bMBQEzWd1U3EtCk9lWAO8zpsIqMzjc2yJnknMON-JmZRCsPfiU0CpT72LvlBaAqsom1IvRs1eZSPYgaw&oh=00_Af48LTGZoSL3Ke67KgsTFqQw3uf9YWHtzSQ1v_5fGQ6s6Q&oe=6A01B0BF	https://www.facebook.com/story.php?story_fbid=122244650408194106&id=233393753185586	\N	\N	t	2025-09-08 01:15:31+08	\N	0	\N	2025-09-08 01:15:31+08	2025-09-08 01:15:31+08	\N	\N	\N	\N	233393753185586_122244650408194106	https://www.facebook.com/story.php?story_fbid=122244650408194106&id=233393753185586	2026-05-07 07:09:04+08
c4144126-6c74-4402-ae0e-54ab4dbdb7af	𝗘𝗫𝗧𝗘𝗡𝗦𝗜𝗢𝗡 𝗗𝗔𝗧𝗘: 𝗝𝗨𝗡𝗘 𝟯𝟬, 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟱	𝗘𝗫𝗧𝗘𝗡𝗦𝗜𝗢𝗡 𝗗𝗔𝗧𝗘: 𝗝𝗨𝗡𝗘 𝟯𝟬, 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟱\n[LOOK] 𝗦𝗲𝗮𝗿𝗰𝗵 𝗳𝗼𝗿 𝟮𝟬𝟮𝟱 𝗖𝗠𝗨 𝗔𝗹𝘂𝗺𝗻𝗶 𝗔𝘄𝗮𝗿𝗱𝗲𝗲𝘀!\nCategories:\n• Golden Jubilarians (Class of 1975)\n• Silver Jubilarians (Class of 2000)\n• Open Category\n🔍 Nominate now! Scan the QR code or visit https://alumni.cmu.edu.ph/\n𝘕𝘰𝘵𝘦: Hard copies must be submitted before or on the deadline of the extension date.\nFor more details,  you may contact \nCMU Alumni Association, Inc. (CMUAAI)/Office of Alumni Relations & Linkages (OARL):\nEmail: cmuaai@cmu.edu.ph\nVisit: CMU Alumni Facebook Page\nCall or Text: 0906 049 3212\nInformation and pubmat from CMUAAI & OARL\n\n[LOOK] Search for 2025 CMU Alumni Awardees!\n\nCategories:\n• Golden Jubilarians (Class of 1975)\n• Silver Jubilarians (Class of 2000)\n• Open Category\n\n🔍 Nominate now! Scan the QR code or visit https://alumni.cmu.edu.ph/\n\nFor more details,  you may contact: \nCMU Alumni Association, Inc. (CMUAAI)/Office of the Alumni Relations & Linkages (OARL) email cmuaai@cmu.edu.ph, call or Text 0906 049 3212.\n\nYou may also visit the CMU Alumni Facebook Page or Fulbright Garden.\n\npubmat by CMUAAI	Update	Medium	All	https://scontent.fcgy3-1.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/487444124_1081416780697315_1319354898036348241_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_p720x720_tt6&_nc_cat=111&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=13d280&_nc_ohc=smbwGXgQaqkQ7kNvwFeXuZ2&_nc_oc=AdpkgsfhIYjMU_FH4EMRD7kZN-cVwrArAZ2N6fpFoCdfvJoso9dbh6iH_UAiWIOLXFQ&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy3-1.fna&edm=AKIiGfEEAAAA&_nc_gid=vkb6lpMGbFtyr5HUL1YbKg&_nc_tpa=Q5bMBQGrxjEfjDRsIAYdt4-cLgsnLS_quOA8Ko9EJLk6RfV7msNuwAA5cJj17ud0MxMWvwSuX2MK3IMq4g&oh=00_Af6sJGzUT1E1kaXnTXIFmYnCSQoRg1yY-fNQTMWrYkCmtw&oe=6A0187FD	https://www.facebook.com/story.php?story_fbid=122216113514194106&id=233393753185586	\N	\N	t	2025-04-03 00:07:27+08	\N	0	\N	2025-04-03 00:07:27+08	2025-04-03 02:31:08+08	\N	\N	\N	\N	233393753185586_122216113514194106	https://www.facebook.com/story.php?story_fbid=122216113514194106&id=233393753185586	2026-05-07