a7e220d8-9783-45aa-af63-1a8885a16f45	𝘼 𝙨𝙩𝙧𝙤𝙣𝙜 𝙥𝙖𝙧𝙩𝙣𝙚𝙧𝙨𝙝𝙞𝙥 𝙬𝙞𝙩𝙝 𝙎𝙩𝙪𝙙𝙚𝙣𝙩 𝘾𝙖𝙢𝙥𝙪𝙨 ?	𝘼 𝙨𝙩𝙧𝙤𝙣𝙜 𝙥𝙖𝙧𝙩𝙣𝙚𝙧𝙨𝙝𝙞𝙥 𝙬𝙞𝙩𝙝 𝙎𝙩𝙪𝙙𝙚𝙣𝙩 𝘾𝙖𝙢𝙥𝙪𝙨 𝙅𝙤𝙪𝙧𝙣𝙖𝙡𝙞𝙨𝙩𝙨 𝙛𝙤𝙧 𝙖 𝙨𝙩𝙧𝙤𝙣𝙜𝙚𝙧 𝘾𝙈𝙐 𝙘𝙤𝙢𝙢𝙪𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙮!\n\nOn February 12, 2026, at the Office of the President Conference Room, Atty. James M. Violon gathered all student campus journalists from the various colleges of the University, including The Central Post, the official student publication of Central Mindanao University.\n\nRecognizing the vital role of student journalists in shaping narratives and mobilizing the community, Atty. Violon underscored their crucial contribution in advancing and promoting the upcoming Alumni Homecoming. Through a strategically established mechanism, student writers will highlight the various events, the University’s preparations, and the initiatives of the CMU Alumni Associations leading up to the much-anticipated celebration.\n\nMore importantly, Atty. Violon successfully earned the commitment of student writers across the University, reiterating how they can better channel their talents and skills in ways that advance CMU’s interests and strengthen alumni relations.\n\nThis initiative marks a meaningful collaboration that promises a more informed, engaged, and united CMU community. Indeed, a partnership that holds great promise for a better and stronger CMU for all.\n\n#CMUAlumniHomecoming2026\n#StudentJournalistsForCMU\n#TheCentralPost\n#OARLInitiative\n#StrongerCMUCommunity\n#OneCMU\n#AdvancingCMU\n\nPhotos from CMU Office of the Alumni Relations and Linkages's post	Update	Medium	All	https://scontent.fcgy3-2.fna.fbcdn.net/v/t39.30808-6/631448411_122269179896194106_1939991280758405293_n.jpg?stp=dst-jpg_p720x720_tt6&_nc_cat=110&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=13d280&_nc_ohc=nKGxbD6WtmEQ7kNvwFTcrP8&_nc_oc=AdqU88TLYU5HBgIT7idSagbi9Sk-ifjbsSV53VYPNScK_aFExWTReamShVWF12Bq2Xg&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent.fcgy3-2.fna&edm=AKIiGfEEAAAA&_nc_gid=vkb6lpMGbFtyr5HUL1YbKg&_nc_tpa=Q5bMBQHtV1hieYbYmt5sRGWe6k3nx3Bll4copYLEePCntyG3U08WOomFYumlPgk37QFwTAJiccfzv