dca4d04b-efb9-43da-9574-81c6be5c4595	𝗢𝗔𝗥𝗟 𝗘𝗮𝗿𝗻𝘀 𝗣𝗼𝘀𝗶𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲 𝗢𝗯𝘀𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗶𝗻 𝗜𝗦𝗢 𝟵𝟬𝟬𝟭:𝟮𝟬𝟭𝟱 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁, 𝗛𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗘?	𝗢𝗔𝗥𝗟 𝗘𝗮𝗿𝗻𝘀 𝗣𝗼𝘀𝗶𝘁𝗶𝘃𝗲 𝗢𝗯𝘀𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻 𝗶𝗻 𝗜𝗦𝗢 𝟵𝟬𝟬𝟭:𝟮𝟬𝟭𝟱 𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝘁, 𝗛𝗶𝗴𝗵𝗹𝗶𝗴𝗵𝘁𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗘𝘅𝗰𝗲𝗹𝗹𝗲𝗻𝗰𝗲 𝗶𝗻 𝗔𝗹𝘂𝗺𝗻𝗶 𝗘𝗻𝗴𝗮𝗴𝗲𝗺𝗲𝗻𝘁 𝗮𝗻𝗱 𝗖𝗼𝗺𝗺𝘂𝗻𝗶𝘁𝘆 𝗦𝗲𝗿𝘃𝗶𝗰𝗲\n\n𝐉𝐔𝐒𝐓 𝐈𝐍 | 𝐅𝐞𝐛𝐫𝐮𝐚𝐫𝐲 𝟐𝟎, 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟔\n\n𝗧Ü𝗩 𝗦Ü𝗗 𝗣𝗦𝗕 𝗣𝗵𝗶𝗹𝗶𝗽𝗽𝗶𝗻𝗲𝘀 has recommended the maintenance of Central Mindanao University’s 𝗜𝗦𝗢 𝟵𝟬𝟬𝟭:𝟮𝟬𝟭𝟱 Certification, reaffirming the University’s sustained compliance with international quality management standards and its deep institutional commitment to excellence in governance and public service.\n\nThe audit results reflect a strong and steadily improving quality management system. The University received eleven (11) Opportunities for Improvement and two (2) positive observations. Notably, Central Mindanao University incurred no non-conformities in the audit, a significant outcome that underscores the robustness of its systems, the discipline of its processes, and the collective dedication of its offices and personnel to quality assurance.\n\nOne of the two positive observations was attributed to the 𝐎𝐟𝐟𝐢𝐜𝐞 𝐨𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐀𝐥𝐮𝐦𝐧𝐢 𝐑𝐞𝐥𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧𝐬 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐋𝐢𝐧𝐤𝐚𝐠𝐞𝐬. This commendation was recorded as a single consolidated observation encompassing two related aspects of the Office’s leadership and program implementation.\n\nThe first aspect recognized the impactful initiatives carried out in the previous year. The auditors cited the Office’s sustained community-oriented programs, including feeding initiatives, brain-boosting activities for learners, libreng tuli operations, and other outreach undertakings that directly benefitted surrounding communities. These initiatives were spearheaded by the 𝐟𝐨𝐫𝐦𝐞𝐫 𝐎𝐀𝐑𝐋 𝐃𝐢𝐫𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐨𝐫, 𝐏𝐫𝐨𝐟. 𝐂𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐢𝐞 𝐋𝐚𝐛𝐧𝐨𝐭𝐢𝐧, in close partnership with the CMU Alumni Association Inc., demonstrating how alumni engagement can meaningfully translate into service to society.\n\nThe second aspect of the same positive observation highlighted the strong planning and forward-looking initiatives prepared for the current year under the leadership of the 𝐧𝐞𝐰 𝐎𝐀𝐑𝐋 𝐃𝐢𝐫𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐨𝐫, 𝐀𝐭𝐭𝐲. 𝐉𝐚𝐦𝐞𝐬 𝐌. 𝐕𝐢𝐨𝐥𝐨𝐧. Together with a committed team of OARL staff members, coordinators, and focal persons, and in collaboration with the CMU Alumni Association Inc. led by 𝗗𝗿. 𝗠𝗮𝗿𝗶𝗮 𝗟𝘂𝘇 𝗦𝗼𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗻𝗼, the Office has developed a dynamic calendar of programs aimed at strengthening alumni relations and institutional pride. These efforts are fully supported by the CMU Administration under the leadership of 𝐔𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐢𝐭𝐲 𝐏𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐧𝐭 𝐃𝐫. 𝐑𝐨𝐥𝐢𝐭𝐨 𝐆. 𝐄𝐛𝐚𝐥𝐥𝐞.\n\nAmong the major events slated for this year are:\n\n𝐊𝐀𝐋𝐀𝐘𝐎: 𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝟏𝐬𝐭 𝐂𝐌𝐔 𝐅𝐥𝐚𝐦𝐞𝐅𝐞𝐬𝐭 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟔\nA student–alumni mass dance competition celebrating unity and school spirit.\n\n𝐁𝐈𝐃𝐋𝐈𝐒𝐈𝐖: 𝐀𝐥𝐮𝐦𝐧𝐢 𝐇𝐨𝐦𝐞𝐜𝐨𝐦𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐋𝐢𝐯𝐞 𝐂𝐨𝐧𝐜𝐞𝐫𝐭 𝐒𝐩𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐚𝐜𝐮𝐥𝐚𝐫\nA night of music, lights, and shared CMU pride.\n\n𝐌𝐱. 𝐂𝐌𝐔 𝐏𝐫𝐢𝐝𝐞 𝐑𝐨𝐲𝐚𝐥𝐞 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟔\nAn inclusive alumni coronation night honoring diversity and confidence.\n\n𝐌𝐢𝐬𝐬 𝐂𝐌𝐔 𝐀𝐥𝐥-𝐒𝐭𝐚𝐫𝐬: 𝐀𝐥𝐮𝐦𝐧𝐢 𝐋𝐞𝐠𝐞𝐧𝐝𝐬 𝐄𝐝𝐢𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟔\nThe grand return of past CMU queens in celebration of legacy and excellence.\n\n𝐏𝐔𝐊𝐒𝐀𝐀𝐍: 𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝐆𝐫𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐅𝐥𝐨𝐚𝐭 𝐂𝐚𝐫𝐧𝐢𝐯𝐚𝐥\nA vibrant college and alumni showdown showcasing creativity and camaraderie.\n\n𝐓𝐡𝐞 𝟏𝐬𝐭 𝐂𝐌𝐔 𝐒𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐞𝐧𝐭–𝐀𝐥𝐮𝐦𝐧𝐢 𝐅𝐢𝐥𝐦 𝐅𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐢𝐯𝐚𝐥 𝟐𝟎𝟐𝟔\nA showcase of storytelling that strengthens the shared legacy of the University.\n\nWith zero non-conformities recorded for the University and no negative observations for the Office of the Alumni Relations and Linkages, the audit results affirm that Central Mindanao University continues to embody excellence in leadership, management, and community engagement.\n\nThese outcomes stand as a testament to a University that does not merely comply with standards but lives them through continuity of leadership, collaboration across offices, and a shared commitment to quality that benefits both the institution and the communities it serves.\n\n#ᴄᴍᴜQᴜᴀʟɪᴛʏᴀꜱꜱᴜʀᴇᴅ #ɪꜱᴏ90012015 #Qᴜᴀʟɪᴛʏᴍᴀɴᴀɢᴇᴍᴇɴᴛ #ᴄᴍᴜᴇxᴄᴇʟʟᴇɴᴄᴇ #ᴏᴀʀʟ #ᴀʟᴜᴍɴɪᴇɴɢᴀɢᴇᴍᴇɴᴛ #ᴘᴜʙʟɪᴄꜱᴇʀᴠɪᴄᴇ #ᴄᴍᴜᴄᴏᴍᴍᴜɴɪᴛʏ #ᴀᴄᴀᴅᴇᴍɪᴄᴇxᴄᴇʟʟᴇɴᴄᴇ #ʟᴇᴀᴅᴇʀꜱʜɪᴘɪɴᴀᴄᴛɪᴏɴ\n\nPhotos from CMU Office of 