74653334-7152-43b0-81ff-5a4c2ae65c05	✨ 𝙊𝘼𝙍𝙇 𝙨𝙩𝙧𝙚𝙣𝙜𝙩𝙝𝙚𝙣𝙨 𝙩𝙝𝙚 𝙘𝙖𝙡𝙡 𝙩𝙤 𝙧𝙚𝙘𝙤𝙣𝙣𝙚𝙘𝙩, 𝙧𝙚𝙪𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚, 𝙖𝙣𝙙 𝙧𝙚𝙞𝙜𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚 𝙩𝙝𝙚 𝘾𝙈𝙐 𝙖𝙡𝙪𝙢𝙣𝙞 𝙨𝙥𝙞𝙧𝙞𝙩! ✨	✨ 𝙊𝘼𝙍𝙇 𝙨𝙩𝙧𝙚𝙣𝙜𝙩𝙝𝙚𝙣𝙨 𝙩𝙝𝙚 𝙘𝙖𝙡𝙡 𝙩𝙤 𝙧𝙚𝙘𝙤𝙣𝙣𝙚𝙘𝙩, 𝙧𝙚𝙪𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚, 𝙖𝙣𝙙 𝙧𝙚𝙞𝙜𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚 𝙩𝙝𝙚 𝘾𝙈𝙐 𝙖𝙡𝙪𝙢𝙣𝙞 𝙨𝙥𝙞𝙧𝙞𝙩! ✨\n\nIn preparation for the upcoming Central Mindanao University Alumni Homecoming this September, the Office of Alumni Relations and Linkages (OARL), today, February 2, 2026, through its Director, Atty. James M. Violon has initiated a purposeful partnership with the various student publications across the University.\n\nThis collaborative initiative aims to encourage and inspire student publication bodies to actively take part in the University-wide drive to reach out to CMU alumni across the Philippines and around the world. Through features, stories, and creative content highlighting CMU initiatives, alumni accomplishments, and notable CMU graduates, student publications will play a key role in strengthening alumni engagement and widening the Homecoming’s impact.\n\nAtty. Violon emphasized that reconnecting with our alumni is not the work of one office alone, but a shared responsibility and honor of the entire CMU community. With this, he expressed a clear direction to tap everyone in the University to strengthen the collective advocacy to:\n\n💛 Reconnect\n💚 Reunite\n🔥 Reignite the CMU spirit of community and excellence among our alumni.\n\nLet us move as one CMU community and make this coming Alumni Homecoming a meaningful celebration of identity, loyalty, and pride in our beloved University.\n\n📣 To all CMU alumni: See you this September!\n\n#CMUAlumniHomecoming2026\n#ReconnectReuniteReignite\n#OARLInitiatives\n#CMUStudentPublications\n#CMUProud\n\n✨ 𝙊𝘼𝙍𝙇 𝙨𝙩𝙧𝙚𝙣𝙜𝙩𝙝𝙚𝙣𝙨 𝙩𝙝𝙚 𝙘𝙖𝙡𝙡 𝙩𝙤 𝙧𝙚𝙘𝙤𝙣𝙣𝙚𝙘𝙩, 𝙧𝙚𝙪𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚, 𝙖𝙣𝙙 𝙧𝙚𝙞𝙜𝙣𝙞𝙩𝙚 𝙩𝙝𝙚 𝘾𝙈𝙐 𝙖𝙡𝙪𝙢𝙣𝙞 𝙨𝙥𝙞𝙧𝙞𝙩! ✨\n\nIn preparation for the upcoming Central Mindanao University Alumni Homecoming this September, the Office of Alumni Relations and Linkages (OARL), today, February 2, 2026, through its Director, Atty. James M. Violon ha